            "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+3y&=1\\\\4x+5y&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$(x,y)=(-1,1)$.",
              "worked": "Subtract the first equation from the second, then substitute $x=-y$ into the first equation.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+2y&=0\\\\x+y&=0\\\\x&=-y\\\\2(-y)+3y&=1\\\\y&=1\\\\x&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $(x,y)=(-1,1)$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 84
          },
          {
            "id": "p22-q18-a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}2x+3y&=2\\\\4x+5y&=2\\end{aligned}$$",
